@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "project.details"

Feature: Project Details
	Testing the Project Details portlet.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.customer2                       |
	| Email Address | pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer2                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pjd.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PJD                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I assign a user the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Manager" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen PJD Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENPJDA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	* I assign a user the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENPJDA"
	* I assign a user the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Watcher" to the project with the code "ZENPJDA"
	* I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENPJDA"
	* I add an order with the product "Digital Enterprise Production" and support level "Platinum" to the project code "ZENPJDA"
	* I add an order with the product "Liferay Commerce Connectors Production" and support level "Floating" to the project code "ZENPJDA"

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen PJD Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I tear down the partner workers with the following email addresses for the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENPJDA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken   |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen PJD Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View project
	New projects created in PJD should be visible in the project details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	Then the project details with the following values should be visible
	| Project Code    | ZENPJDA         |
	| Status          | APPROVED        |
	| Level           | Platinum        |
	| Support Region  | US              |
	| Partner         | Zen OSB Partner |
	| Partner Support | Yes             |
	| Tier            | Premier         |
	| Industry        | Automotive      |
	| Last Modified   | Today           |
	| Modified By     | Amos Fong       |
	When I go to the Team Members tab
	Then the team member with the name "PJD Customer1" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | PJD Customer1                       |
	| Role  | Developer                           |
	| Email | pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	And the team member with the name "PJD Customer2" should be visible with the following values
	| Name  | PJD Customer2                       |
	| Role  | Watcher                             |
	| Email | pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	When I go to the Offerings tab
	Then the offering with the product name "Portal Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Portal Production |
	| SLA              | Gold              |
	| Start Date       | Today             |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now   |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 10000         |
	| Tickets          | Unlimited         |
	| Version          | 6                 |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1          |
	| Status           | ACTIVE            |
	And the offering with the product name "Digital Enterprise Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Digital Enterprise Production |
	| SLA              | Platinum                      |
	| Start Date       | Today                         |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now               |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 1                         |
	| Tickets          | Unlimited                     |
	| Version          | 7                             |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                      |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                        |
	And the offering with the product name "Liferay Commerce Connectors Production" should be visible with the following values
	| Product          | Liferay Commerce Connectors Production |
	| SLA              | Floating                               |
	| Start Date       | Today                                  |
	| Support End Date | 1 year from now                        |
	| Licenses         | 0 / 0                                  |
	| Tickets          | 0                                      |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                               |
	| Status           | ACTIVE                                 |
	When I go to the History tab
	Then the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | Role              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Developer         |
	And the history entry in position number "1" with the field value "User" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | User              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | PJD Customer1     |
	And the history entry in position number "2" with the field value "Role" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | Role              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | Watcher           |
	And the history entry in position number "2" with the field value "User" should be visible with the following values
	| Updater Name                | Amos Fong         |
	| Update Summary              | Assigned Customer |
	| Update Date                 | Today             |
	| Update Field Name           | User              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A               |
	| Update Field New Value      | PJD Customer2     |

Scenario: Add portal environment details
	Users should be able to add portal environment details via the Project Details page.

	Given I go to the Project Details page
	And I search for the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I go to the project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive"
	And I add an environment configuration with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |
	Then the environment configuration with the name "Zen Portal Environment One" should be visible with the following values
	| Name               | Zen Portal Environment One |
	| Product            | Portal Production          |
	| Liferay Version    | 6.2 EE                     |
	| Operating System   | Windows Server 2012        |
	| Java Version       | Oracle JDK 7               |
	| Application Server | Tomcat 7.0                 |
	| Database           | MariaDB 10.0               |
	| Cloud Services     | Azure SQL Databases        |
	| Browser            | Chrome                     |
	| Portal EXT         | portal-ext.properties      |
	| Patch Info         | patchinfo.txt              |

