Scenario: View project offerings as customer and partner
	Projects created in PJD should have certain elements visible to customers and partners in the project details page.

	Given I edit a project with the name "Zen PJD Automotive" and code "ZENPJDA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product "Portal Production"
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I update the support password for user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to "osbadminqauser"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.customer2@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	And I assign the support user with the email address "pjd.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" to the support group "Help Center"
	When I log out and log into the support homepage as "pjd.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "osbadminqauser"
	And I go to the Project Details page
	And I go to the Offerings tab
